  "notes": "Drawn from the Dec 2025 photo of N8619F (left side). The engine is mostly hidden behind the shield and wing in it: maroon by what shows (low confidence). The eagle (head, banner, wings with their black feather strokes, olive leaves, blue feather tips and the rising sun) and the shield are logos, apps draw them as art; re-measured 2026-11-28 on the January 2023 left photo of N8619F (MIA), the right side mirrored as the September 2023 right photo shows. The shield's point and the olive leaves carry on over the left engine's cowl, not drawn there. Re-checked 2026-11-15: the fin is the state jets' Heart fin as re-measured on Colorado One (the same fin on every 737), copied with its 'Southwest' title and flag. 'Illinois One' measured on the December 2025 left photo against the nose and the forward door (1.9-3.3 m back), two weights, a pair of titles per side (the right mirrored: both photos are of the left side), on Colorado One's line under the cockpit windows. The rising sun's round edge made smooth; the eagle, shield and banner are art drawn as polygons with real corners.",
  "history": "Previously on N918WN."
